			"date": "2024-07-17T14:12:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Personally, I’d like to see a law that says every hardware device company must plan for obsolescence and failure before releasing a product. This includes open-sourcing services in the case of failure.</p><p>Also, they must account for the recycling or decommissioning of their products in terms of the price of their products.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
