		{
			"id": "112802508889689338",
			"parentId": "112802343452015638",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/112802508635510893",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-17T15:21:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The​ framing of \"guest friendly\" really seals the deal: if you're making stuff nobody else will ever need to use, sure, go ham. But if other people will be using what you build, the bar goes *way* up.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112802567969766215",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://logoff.website/@jason/112802567943120973",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jason Petersen (he)",
				"url": "https://logoff.website/@jason",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/735/769/398/007/030/original/10f1455d521e0150.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-17T15:36:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> you mean internet outage, not power, right?</p><p>I have a couple of UPSes in my house but I’m not sure what exactly my home automation is expected to do when the power’s out. Lights? HVAC? My coffee maker? They all don’t work without power.</p><p>And yeah, don’t use devices that talk over the internet.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112802573576866358",
			"parentId": "112802567969766215",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112802573576866358",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-17T15:37:55.917Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://logoff.website/@jason\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jason</span></a></span> no I did not originally mean that but both failure modes are important!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112802592195698987",
			"parentId": "112802573576866358",
			"url": "https://logoff.website/@jason/112802592156370827",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jason Petersen (he)",
				"url": "https://logoff.website/@jason",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/735/769/398/007/030/original/10f1455d521e0150.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-17T15:42:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I like your analogy. My automation use is in the “progressive enhancement” mode. Wall switches, thermostats, etc all just work with no automation. People come in and don’t even realize anything is automated, everything seems normal.</p><p>I’ll have to keep this as a principle going forward (it always has been, because of guests and parents and such)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
