			},
			"date": "2024-07-17T16:48:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> yeah, you gotta be extremely careful to buy “progressively enhanced” smart home stuff, and it's sometimes hard to tell how something is designed without just trying it out. It's ridiculous how many things flat out *need* to talk to a server instead of being able to send/receive commands on your local network if all the devices are on it.</p>",
